  "answer": "### Short Answer\nNo, the deadline to file an income tax return is not the same as the deadline to file a protest to an assessment. The income tax return must be filed annually, while a protest to an assessment must be filed within a specific period after the assessment notice is received.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nPractically, this means that taxpayers must be vigilant about two separate deadlines: one for their annual income tax return and another for any disputes regarding assessments. Failure to file the income tax return by April 15 can result in penalties, while missing the 30-day window to protest an assessment can lead to the loss of the right to contest the tax due. Taxpayers should maintain awareness of both timelines to ensure compliance and protect their rights.",
